id: pm-brief-vc49
title: Reconcile the corrupt-receipt fixture comment with what the pinned SDK now does
description: "Greptile flagged on pull request 100 that the fixture setup carried two contradictory explanations of the same receipts. The first comment stated that the SDK pushes both incomplete receipts and then throws while sorting by created_at, and that one receipt would not do because the comparator is never invoked on a single-element array. The second comment, added when the pin moved to 2026.8.30, stated that the SDK now drops those same receipts and returns an empty array. Both were true at different times and neither said so, leaving conflicting accounts of why the fixture needs a pair. Reworded the first comment to name the throwing path as the original behaviour up to 2026.8.12, to state plainly that the pinned 2026.8.30 returns an empty array for this exact fixture, and to say why the pair is retained anyway: it is the only shape that reaches every handling the SDK has had, so the fixture stays valid whichever one a future version picks. No assertion changed and no behaviour changed. Suite 353 of 353 pass and typecheck is clean."
type: Chore
